# Always commit and push after work

When a task that changes the repo is finished, create a git commit and push to GitHub (`origin`) unless the user explicitly says not to.

- Follow the repo's commit message style (concise, why-focused).
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, `*.creds`, Snapcraft credentials, tokens).
- After a successful commit, push the current branch (`git push -u origin HEAD` if needed).
- Do not force-push to main/master unless the user explicitly asks.
- If the only leftover is secret/untracked junk, still commit and push the real code changes and leave secrets untracked.
